  ('zcrm_1579374000011741049', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011862262', 'Pete Scifo', NULL, '12-13-17 He''s with Kaiser now for last 5 years. Now going up to $793 a month with high ded. Healthy, non-smoker, pre-diabetic, 3-4 x year takes blood panel but no meds. Have not shared pre-x clause because he had to go to daughter''s or granddaughter''s concert.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2017-12-13 18:03:54', '2017-12-13 18:03:54'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000011741044', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000001659002', 'Dorothy Fears', NULL, '12-13-17 She wanted to know difference between HEP and HES. I told her and she''s going to think it over. Byron has turned 65 so he''s on Medicare now. So, price is nearly the same. She does want to go to a dermatologist to get her skin checked. Otherwise sees naturopath for gut thing and doesn''t submit to anyone. Told her same pre-x clause for both companies. Also has own chiro, dentist and eye dr. not willing to change. Referred Jim and Anne Lelong but I think they went directly to LHS perhaps. I see no sign of them and she gave them my name. Ho hum.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2017-12-13 17:39:26', '2017-12-13 17:39:26'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000011741039', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011779272', 'Ernest Bruss III', NULL, '12-13-17 Please note (Ernest) Chip Bruss is in CRM already and will need to be merged!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2017-12-13 17:05:54', '2017-12-13 17:05:54'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000011741034', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011744066', 'Tawnya Charlson', NULL, '12-13-17 Chose to not get insurance at all most likely. Not worth it to her. She''s going to risk going without since costs so much. Cheaper to pay penalty then pay for monthly cost since she never goes to doctor.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2017-12-13 17:02:27', '2017-12-13 17:02:27'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000011741026', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011752368', 'Jill Fields', NULL, '12-13-17 Jill is 44 and has husband and 2 kids. Husband and 2 kids are on Freedom Life for $400 which does not include annual wellness visits. Jill had thyroid removed this year so no chance of cancer, biopsy all clear. She has high cholesterol and takes Zocor for cheap. Also takes Armourthyroid which looks like $40 or so. Might be cheaper with World Meds, not sure. They are going to run the numbers and determine if makes sense to keep low level of Freedom Life for Jill and HEP/Sedera to give her the co-pay for the doctor visits for the blood work and such. Sent her the application. Want to decide in next day or so.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2017-12-13 16:57:54', '2017-12-13 16:58:13'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000011741018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011862440', 'Robert (Greg) White', NULL, '12-13-17 By chance he heard Tyson Van Landingham talk with me and his client on the phone the other day! Greg couldn''t believe it! He got nervous I''d connect the dots, not that it matters. Greg wishes Tyson would just offer Sedera to their entire group of employees. But, if that happens it will be slow in making it happen.  Completed application just now with me on phone. All set!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2017-12-13 15:32:36', '2017-12-13 15:34:54'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000011747013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011809309', 'Kyle Simpson', NULL, '12-13-17   Kyle wishes to pay quarterly payments.  1st payment use bank information for first 3mo payment.  Bill 2,3,4 payment by invoice.', 'Ron Patterson', 'Ron Patterson', '2017-12-13 15:27:19', '2017-12-13 15:27:19'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000011747008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011809309', 'Kyle Simpson', NULL, '12-13-17  Received call from Kyle.  He went to seminar that Sedera held and listen to a group presentation.  They told him to call us.  He basically had good knowledge about cost sharing and Sedera.  I explained our side of the program.  He kept asking if he didn''t like the program how he could exit.  Then he explained how he believes COBRA works and he felt if he quits or plan he should be allowed to get on health insurance.  I told him that Qualifying Events do not work as he believes.  I consulted with Patti and she spoke with him to and told him the same.  Next he said "well if you fire me as a sub-contractor" than I can get it.  Why can''t you do that so I can get coverage.  He got disconnect and he called back claiming he was spoken to rudely and unprofessionally and had the right to ask questions. I calmed him down, answered all his other questions and he then said he was ready to enroll.  I took him to enrollment platform and he enrolled.  I hope I get paid the MAX on this one, I really took one for the team!!!!', 'Ron Patterson', 'Ron Patterson', '2017-12-13 15:12:14', '2017-12-13 15:12:14'),
