  ('zcrm_1579374000011247013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011910001', 'John Singleton', NULL, 'I got your number from Jesse Chatham.  He said you might have some health care options for our family.  We are both self employed and our care went from $939 to $1589 a month for Cigna Bronze HSA 6500.  So it doesn''t even pay for anything until we have paid $6500 deductible.  So I feel like we are paying 25K a year and then coverage kicks in.  I have been thinking of going no insurance but catastrophic and just paying out of pocket. Since we are done having babies, etc., I am thinking this makes sense.  Jesse told me about this plan that might be an option.  Can you go in to details about it?  




Here is our family-  Anne Singleton 8/16/74 John Singleton 7/29/73  John Campbell Singleton 9/12/12 Tison Philip Singleton 7/16/14 and Willa Anne Singleton 2/4/17.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2017-11-29 12:05:07', '2017-11-29 12:05:07'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000011247008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011508132', 'Paul Dart', NULL, 'Completed application just now for him and his wife. He currently has a non-compliant plan paying $584 a month. They thought the regulation would go away. So, now wants a compliant plan so they aren''t penalized. Super healthy, totally alternative treatments, homeopathic, don''t use Western medicine. Had HSA but no longer. Choosing $1000/$485 and Jan. 1st start date.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2017-11-29 11:32:36', '2017-11-29 11:32:36'),
