  ('zcrm_1579374000007689003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000000518266', 'Daniela Dadurian, M.D.', NULL, '05.23.17:  Patti recvd. email from Jennifer Carbone asking what $50 monthly fee is for.  Called - spoke w/Jennifer, explained fee.  She didn''t know if the fee had to do with the practice or if it was personal.  She is ok with it.', 'Joan Phelps', 'Joan Phelps', '2017-05-23 11:19:49', '2017-05-23 11:19:49'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000007648007', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000007494001', 'Carlos Gamiz', NULL, '05.19.17:  Emailed Carlos re: referral fees lowering his monthly share fee.', 'Joan Phelps', 'Joan Phelps', '2017-05-19 12:55:25', '2017-05-19 12:55:25'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000007655003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000005011193', 'Andre Mpitsos', NULL, '5-19-17 Chose the $299 level + $125 start up.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2017-05-19 10:29:54', '2017-05-19 10:29:54'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000007653003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000007494001', 'Carlos Gamiz', NULL, '05.18.17:  Carlos called - said he didn''t receive my email. Re-sent it. After reviewing Sedera info., he liked program but family share fee is too high.  Said he will research further and get back to me.', 'Joan Phelps', 'Joan Phelps', '2017-05-19 10:21:30', '2017-05-19 10:21:30'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000007648003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000005041285', 'Terry Bickel', NULL, 'We called and went inactive with Liberty HealthShare about a month ago. I''ve gone onto employer coverage. Please cease all attempts to collect payments from my credit card. Thank you', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2017-05-19 09:06:53', '2017-05-19 09:06:53'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000007626061', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000008973067', 'Megan Yost', NULL, '5-18-17 Sent to me by Kimberly Homer. They are neighbors. Megan''s only health issue is mild depression and takes generic of Cymbalta called Duloxetine. Priced low with coupon on GoodRX for $18 - $20 for 30mg/30 days. Super pricey on WeRX. Don''t use that site.  She sees Dr. Gerald Chitters about 6-8 times a year and was worried about that co-pay which is about $150 if she pays cash. Sedera is the best option as long as drug prices with coupon are still low. She wants to enroll in Aug. for a Sept 1st start date. She''s riding out Medicaid for as long as she can. Starting new job on Monday though. Her new employer does not offer healthcare but will pay $300 a month towards healthcare! We have Aug. 2nd set for an appointment to enroll. Allowed for 1 hour.  C4HCO plans started at $318 on up for plans in which none had co-pays for any mental health. So, she''d pay full amount either way for all of those visits.  Remind her that mental health is NOT shared with Sedera at any point. But, gets 3 free consultations through their network.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2017-05-18 17:11:17', '2017-05-18 17:14:09'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000007629023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000005998313', 'Sergio Medina', NULL, 'This member has never paid since inception.  I will cancel.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2017-05-18 14:49:30', '2017-05-18 14:49:30'),
