  ('zcrm_1579374000007276011', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000003037119', 'Mary Ellen Metke', NULL, '4-18-17 WS - By chance I accepted the Big Wave Lead and it''s a current HES member of John Vnuk''s. She''s frustrated bc BCH won''t accept her card. I explained how it works as a self-pay patient and gave her the Concierge''s phone number to help her sort out her bill from back in Aug that she Just got a bill for and they are threatening to send her to collections even though she just received the bill. She''s been a member since last July.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2017-04-18 11:30:27', '2017-04-18 11:31:58'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000007276007', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000006435105', 'Sheri Kessler', NULL, '4-18-17 Please cancel per this email, "Hello Liberty and My Academy of Health Excellence Select,

Although I was grateful to be accepted into the Health Excellence Select and Liberty HealthShare Program, I unfortunately decided that I will need to cancel my membership, which was scheduled to begin on May 1, 2017.

Thank you so much, Wendy, for all that you did with helping me to get on board.  I VERY MUCH appreciate all of your hard work and apologize for not going forth with my membership.

Perhaps I will sign up at a later date, and if so, I realize I will need to go through the enrollment process again at that time.
Is there anything else I should be aware of if I decide to enroll in the future?

You probably want to know the reason for my canceling at this time.....
Although I feel like the concept is an awesome one and I hope more and more people decide to take this path to health care, I just didn''t feel quite comfortable with the bottom line idea that:
This program does not guarantee or promise that your medical bills will be paid or assigned to others for payment. Whether anyone chooses to pay your medical bills will be totally voluntary. As such, this program should never be considered as a substitute for an insurance policy. Whether you receive any payments for medical expenses and whether or not this program continues to operate, you are always liable for any unpaid bills. 

I think another factor was that I would also prefer not to have to pay upfront for any potential exams and/or lab tests.

I have paid for the Health Excellence Select fee of $25, as well as Liberty''s annual membership fee of $135.
I am asking that those fees be refunded at your convenience.

Please let me know that you have received this mail and are processing the request.....and if you have any other questions."', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2017-04-18 11:18:32', '2017-04-18 11:18:32'),
