  ('zcrm_1579374000006536007', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000006532103', 'Gabriella Zettelmeyer', NULL, 'Per Phillip this member did not complete the CC info.  I will convert and make status Liberty only.  2 attempts at getting CC no response.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2017-02-24 12:52:41', '2017-02-24 12:52:41'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000006536003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000003037159', 'Heidi Stabler', NULL, 'This is Heidi Stabler, I have a policy with liberty health share account number 142234588.  I would like to cancel my policy because my husband is now a full time employee at a company that offers health insurance benefits.  The company is pay a good portion of the health insurance so it will cut the cost of what we pay each month.  
We have enjoyed this company and if it wasn''t for the company paying a good portion of the insurance we would have stayed with Liberty Health Share. 

Thank you and if you have any other questions please email.

Heidi Stabler', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2017-02-24 10:58:33', '2017-02-24 10:58:33'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000006527012', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000005185086', 'Michelle Gossen', NULL, 'Called in asking about contacting doc and wellfit registration, gave info, sent email and invitation.', 'MPB Health Member Notification', 'MPB Health Member Notification', '2017-02-24 10:41:51', '2017-02-24 10:41:51'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000006502003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000005518003', 'David Proverb', NULL, 'Hello Patti,
Please accept this letter of cancellation of my policy with your company.  I don''t know my policy number.
The reason for cancellation is because I never requested this coverage!  My girlfriend contacted Debi Pender back in November.  Debi advised her to sign up with Liberty Healthshare.  After sending her a link to do so, my girlfriend, Lisa,  filled out the information, sent it to Liberty and after waiting two weeks for our enrollment to show up on their records and calling them ourselves, Liberty advised us to go ahead and go directly to their website and try signing up again.  We signed up again, on our own, and got it all done.
Debi''s assistance in all this only consisted on one phone call we made to her, she sending a link, and we did all the rest from filling out all the paperwork, to following up several times with Liberty to ensure our enrollment.  Then after all was done we both realized that we had been charged by your company for these policies which were never explained to us, nor was your company EVER authorized to not only charge my credit card, but also charge Lisa''s as well.  
We still don''t know how your company got my credit card information?  Lisa also called in and cancelled, and has since been reimbursed for the 25.00 plus 50.00 for a total of 75.00.  Therefore, I am also demanding a refund of my 75.00 charged to my credit card immediately.  It is a Wells Fargo Visa account ending in 7936.  The charges were made on 12/22 for 25.00 and 1/05 for 50.00.
I will be looking for this refund on my statement to be made upon receipt of this letter.  If anymore information is needed, please advise.
Please also confirm receipt of this letter.

Regards,

-- 
Dave Proverb
 772.201.7646', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2017-02-22 14:03:42', '2017-02-22 14:03:42'),
