  ('zcrm_1579374000003791011', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000003176005', 'Jennifer Moen', NULL, '8-23-16 Jennifer wrote "I am wondering if I can ask about the definition of a pre-existing condition with Liberty Healthshare that I saw when I started reading the emails.

I remember telling you I wanted to have a baby soon, and you asked if I was already pregnant (no I wasn''t) and so I was accepted into the club.  

Their pre-existing condition clause says anything I was taking a "medication" for is excluded.  does medication include estrogen?  I was taking estrogen since July.  

I had an embryo transfer in Argentina on August 1st and I had two positive tests on the 10th and 12th.  I will need to see a doctor here soon....  I have ppwk to show the procedure was on the first if needed.  

:)

Let me know if there is somewhere I should call or look up.

My friend pointed out that I was taking estrogen to treat infertility but I''m not infertile anymore... just reaching...  lol"
Now looking at regular plans and maybe CO Choice Health.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2016-08-23 21:43:41', '2016-08-23 21:43:41'),
